# Deliberately empty.
#
# textlint auto-loads the repository root's `.textlintignore` for any invocation, and that file
# excludes `examples/sample.md` from this repository's own dogfood lint (its violations are the
# demo, not debt -- see the root file's comment). That exclusion is correct for the ratchet, but it
# also silently empties the walkthrough command in `examples/README.md`, whose entire point is to
# print those violations to a first-time user.
#
# `examples/README.md`'s commands pass `--ignore-path examples/.textlintignore` to opt back out of
# the root file for that one invocation, without weakening the root exclusion for anything else.
# This file has to exist and be empty for that override to work: `--ignore-path` needs a real file,
# and an empty one contributes no patterns of its own.
